From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: L974 chain, reports and MME words keep draw reuse (EDEN_UP_L974_CHAIN)

DRAFT, not built. Ports zortos293/Lichii PR #974 (@mstampfli). Gated by EDEN_UP_L974_CHAIN
(exact 1), a live switch (common/live_switch.h, Id L974Chain, not armed); off by default. It
only changes anything with EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW=1. Report operands, the vertex id base, counter
resets and the render condition become draw parameters; MME memory words 0x154-0x156 only while
macros run on the split's front. Reports that are not fence releases still execute and record
their 4/16-byte destination (NoteFastDrawConstantData); fence releases still end reuse. With
EDEN_NX2_GPU_PROFILE or EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW_VERIFY the 10-second "Fast draw per second:" line gains
"| chained C/N (P%...) | break events: ... | full counts: ...". No buffer work is removed.

Reviewed draft from job J, v2: reviewer re-anchored the live_switch.h Id/kDefs hunks on the T122
tail, made MME words 0x154-0x156 neutral only under FrontMacros() (inline back macros flush
GPU-written memory with no break), read the switch with LiveSwitch::Peek, aligned the
diagnostics flag with ReportFastDraws' condition, and moved maxwell_3d.h comments back.
